# Day 31

## Experiment Title

Understanding Microservices Architecture using Docker Compose


## Objective

To study the basics of microservices architecture and understand how Docker Compose supports microservice based applications.


## Theory

Microservices architecture is a software development approach in which an application is divided into multiple small and independent services. Each service performs a specific task and communicates with other services through networks.

Docker Compose helps in managing microservice based applications by allowing multiple services to run together in isolated containers. It simplifies deployment, scaling, and service communication in modern application development.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and verify that Docker services are running properly.

Create a Docker Compose configuration file containing multiple services.

Configure separate containers for different application components.

Start all services using Docker Compose.

Verify communication between the services through Docker networking.

Inspect the running containers and service configuration.


## Output

Multiple services were deployed successfully using Docker Compose.

Containers communicated properly through the Docker network.

Microservice based application deployment was completed successfully.


## Result

Successfully understood the basics of microservices architecture using Docker Compose.
